{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a2-spain-part-2/audio/main-3bf79ddbbb82.mp3","durationSec":252.024,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":3.06,"text":"When people in Spain meet, they often give dos besos."},{"start":3.66,"end":6.84,"text":"Dos besos is Spanish for two kisses, one on each cheek."},{"start":7.42,"end":8.48,"text":"It is not a real kiss."},{"start":8.88,"end":9.88,"text":"The cheeks just touch."},{"start":10.68,"end":12.56,"text":"People make a small kiss sound in the air."},{"start":13.06,"end":15.62,"text":"Women do this with women, and men do it with women."},{"start":16.42,"end":18.08,"text":"People do it with friends and family."},{"start":18.48,"end":21.2,"text":"They also do it with someone new, like a friend of a friend."},{"start":21.82,"end":23.44,"text":"Two men usually shake hands."},{"start":23.86,"end":26.82,"text":"If they are close friends or family, they often hug."},{"start":27.5,"end":31.32,"text":"At work, more people now shake hands, especially at a first meeting."},{"start":32.24,"end":37,"text":"For Spanish people, the two kisses are a normal, warm hello, like a smile."},{"start":37.44,"end":40.62,"text":"So a Spanish person may feel a little hurt if a visitor steps back."},{"start":41.44,"end":44.8,"text":"Most people in Spain have one first name and two family names."},{"start":45.3,"end":47.54,"text":"The first family name usually comes from the father."},{"start":47.9,"end":49.64,"text":"The second family name comes from the mother."},{"start":50.04,"end":52.62,"text":"So one name shows both sides of the family."},{"start":53.28,"end":55.9,"text":"The famous painter Pablo Picasso shows this."},{"start":56.56,"end":59.26,"text":"His two family names were Ruiz and Picasso."},{"start":59.98,"end":64.28,"text":"Ruiz was his father's family name, and Picasso was his mother's."},{"start":64.58,"end":66.5,"text":"Later, he used only his mother's name."},{"start":67.46,"end":70.42,"text":"When women in Spain marry, they do not change their names."},{"start":71.1,"end":74.02,"text":"They keep the family names from their parents all their lives."},{"start":74.88,"end":77.5,"text":"Today, parents can choose which family name comes first."},{"start":78.22,"end":81.24,"text":"But all the children in one family must have the same order."},{"start":81.84,"end":85.14,"text":"So brothers and sisters always have the same two family names."},{"start":86.1,"end":91.2,"text":"Every March, the city of Valencia has a big festival called Las Fallas."},{"start":91.2,"end":94.02,"text":"Each part of the city makes a falla."},{"start":94.02,"end":96.52,"text":"A falla is a very big group of many figures."},{"start":97.38,"end":100.02,"text":"Each figure in a falla is a ninot."},{"start":100.02,"end":104.5,"text":"Fallas are made of wood and paper, and some are as tall as a building."},{"start":105.02,"end":108.96,"text":"Many are funny, because they make jokes about famous people and the news."},{"start":109.6,"end":113.18,"text":"On the night of 19 March, people burn almost all of them."},{"start":114.56,"end":117.28,"text":"This fire night is called la Cremà."},{"start":117.28,"end":119.24,"text":"Why burn something so beautiful?"},{"start":119.96,"end":123,"text":"The idea comes from carpenters, people who make things from wood."},{"start":123.6,"end":127.84,"text":"In winter, they used old wood to hold candles, so they could work at night."},{"start":128.56,"end":132.06,"text":"At the end of winter, the days got longer, so they burned the old wood."},{"start":132.66,"end":135.58,"text":"They did it on 19 March, the day of Saint Joseph."},{"start":136.26,"end":139.54,"text":"Saint Joseph also worked with wood, so he was special to them."},{"start":141.3,"end":144.9,"text":"Every year, visitors vote for their favourite ninot."},{"start":144.9,"end":147.84,"text":"The winners are saved from the fire and go to a museum."},{"start":150.34,"end":153.98,"text":"The Canary Islands are seven big islands in the Atlantic Ocean."},{"start":154.52,"end":158.44,"text":"They are part of Spain, but only about 100 kilometres from Africa."},{"start":159.22,"end":161.56,"text":"The islands were made by volcanoes."},{"start":162.04,"end":165.42,"text":"The volcano Teide is on Tenerife, the biggest island."},{"start":166.12,"end":167.92,"text":"It is the highest mountain in Spain."},{"start":168.7,"end":173.42,"text":"People call them the islands of eternal spring, a spring that never ends."},{"start":174.4,"end":177.64,"text":"The weather is warm all year, and it does not change much."},{"start":178.92,"end":181.66,"text":"Winters are warm, because the islands are far south."},{"start":182.42,"end":186.1,"text":"In summer, the sea is cool and the wind blows on most days."},{"start":186.86,"end":188.84,"text":"So winter and summer are not very different."},{"start":190.62,"end":194.24,"text":"Camino de Santiago is Spanish for the Way of Saint James."},{"start":194.96,"end":198.14,"text":"It is a long walk to the city of Santiago de Compostela."},{"start":198.72,"end":200.84,"text":"The city is in the north-west of Spain."},{"start":200.84,"end":204.74,"text":"Saint James was one of the first people to follow Jesus."},{"start":205.68,"end":208.46,"text":"People believe he is buried in the big church of the city."},{"start":209.02,"end":212.48,"text":"So for more than a thousand years, pilgrims have walked there."},{"start":213.5,"end":216.88,"text":"Pilgrims are people who travel to a special church or place."},{"start":217.44,"end":221.7,"text":"The most popular way starts in France and is about 800 kilometres long."},{"start":222.36,"end":224.82,"text":"People on the Camino carry a pilgrim passport."},{"start":225.24,"end":228.24,"text":"In each town where they sleep, they get a stamp in it."},{"start":228.72,"end":230.96,"text":"The stamps show where they walked."},{"start":232.1,"end":234.8,"text":"At the end, pilgrims can get the Compostela."},{"start":235.42,"end":237.5,"text":"It is a special paper with their name on it."},{"start":237.78,"end":242.66,"text":"To get it, pilgrims must walk at least the last 100 kilometres."},{"start":242.66,"end":246.1,"text":"On this part, they need at least two stamps every day."},{"start":246.8,"end":251.38,"text":"That is why many people start in Sarria, just over 100 kilometres from Santiago."}],"words":[{"text":"When","start":0,"end":0.18},{"text":"people","start":0.18,"end":0.42},{"text":"in","start":0.42,"end":0.62},{"text":"Spain","start":0.62,"end":0.86},{"text":"meet","start":0.86,"end":1.24},{"text":"they","start":1.54,"end":1.58},{"text":"often","start":1.58,"end":1.88},{"text":"give","start":1.88,"end":2.2},{"text":"dos","start":2.2,"end":2.52},{"text":"besos","start":2.52,"end":3.06},{"text":"Dos","start":3.66,"end":3.8},{"text":"besos","start":3.8,"end":4.28},{"text":"is","start":4.28,"end":4.48},{"text":"Spanish","start":4.48,"end":4.84},{"text":"for","start":4.84,"end":5.14},{"text":"two","start":5.14,"end":5.38},{"text":"kisses","start":5.38,"end":5.7},{"text":"one","start":5.96,"end":6.16},{"text":"on","start":6.16,"end":6.3},{"text":"each","start":6.3,"end":6.5},{"text":"cheek","start":6.5,"end":6.84},{"text":"It","start":7.42,"end":7.5},{"text":"is","start":7.5,"end":7.64},{"text":"not","start":7.64,"end":7.86},{"text":"a","start":7.86,"end":7.98},{"text":"real","start":7.98,"end":8.18},{"text":"kiss","start":8.18,"end":8.48},{"text":"The","start":8.88,"end":8.98},{"text":"cheeks","start":8.98,"end":9.2},{"text":"just","start":9.2,"end":9.52},{"text":"touch","start":9.52,"end":9.88},{"text":"People","start":10.68,"end":10.88},{"text":"make","start":10.88,"end":11.06},{"text":"a","start":11.06,"end":11.24},{"text":"small","start":11.24,"end":11.52},{"text":"kiss","start":11.52,"end":11.78},{"text":"sound","start":11.78,"end":12.08},{"text":"in","start":12.08,"end":12.24},{"text":"the","start":12.24,"end":12.34},{"text":"air","start":12.34,"end":12.56},{"text":